{
  "core_message": "A dead bear became a taxidermied celebrity after eating a million‑dollar dose of cocaine.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "175‑lb Bear Overdosed on $20 Million Worth of Cocaine",
  "description": "A 175‑pound black bear met a fatal fate after consuming a jettisoned cargo of cocaine dropped by smugglers in 1985. The body was taxidermied and now hangs in a Kentucky mall, where it even officiates weddings. \n\nKey points: 40 containers, 75 pounds of cocaine, 3–4 grams absorbed, taxidermy, legal loophole.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Cocaine Bear (bear)\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocaine_Bear_(bear)), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImage credits:\nCocaine Bear, Kentucky for Kentucky Fun Mall (cropped).jpg (Ferrett333, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocaine_Bear,_Kentucky_for_Kentucky_Fun_Mall_(cropped).jpg\n\n3D models:\nBlackBear (everything-animals) by David OReilly (CC BY 4.0) https://davidoreilly.itch.io/everything-library-animals\nCessna-172 by Sousinho (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-8e8d0a8eefe544eea7c5169c1de2d7c9",
